(a) An entity desiring designation as a "qualifying business" or "service enterprise" under this article must apply to the director. An application fee in an amount to be determined by the director shall be required. In addition to other information requested by DeKalb County, the following items shall accompany the application:
(1) A description of business conducted by the applicant at the each location within the enterprise zone;
(2) Documentation reflecting the number of full-time job equivalents maintained by the applicant at the subject location within the enterprise zone as of the date of application, as compared to the number of such full-time job equivalents maintained as of the effective date of this article, and the projected number of full-time job equivalents three (3) years after the proposed investment;
(3) The name and address of each employee occupying each new full-time job at the subject location within the enterprise zone, and a determination of whether each such employee was a low-income or moderate-income individual as of the date of hire for the new full-time job;
(4) Description and documentation of any additional economic stimulus provided within the enterprise zone by the applicant;
(5) A legal description of the property;
(6) Documentation reflecting any expenses incurred in rehabilitation of existing real property and improvements;
(7) Data from the DeKalb County Tax Assessor reflecting the value of the real property and improvements both before and after rehabilitation, if applicable;
(8) Photographic documentation of the real property and improvements both before and after rehabilitation, if applicable.
(b) Falsification of documents, failure to develop the project or comply with any provision of this article may result in revocation of any designation granted and recapture of any and all incentives granted to any otherwise qualifying business or service enterprise.
(Ord. No. 13-02, Pt. I, 12-20-01; Ord. No. 06-15, Pt. I, 9-12-06)

